{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"harmless-wavy-osprey","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nCommit cf5155e528 added the real-pandoc corpus safety suite. Its module promises every test shares one cached render, but functools.lru_cache is process-local and CI uses pytest-xdist -n 3. Runtime instrumentation produced three cache fills, one per worker, while serial produced one. Two post-merge macOS jobs spent 321.6s and 495.6s of aggregate test-call time in five wiki corpus tests; the latter default tier took 33m51s. The tests preserve valuable coverage and must remain real-pandoc, full-corpus checks.\n\n## Plan\nRestructure the corpus oracle so each body/pass is rendered once per pytest session, not once per assertion or xdist worker. Partition by stratum or use a session-scoped shared artifact/lock so no single test breaches the 300s timeout. Preserve cardinality, secret scrub, protected excerpts, tables, comments, determinism, fixed-point, coverage-ratio, and non-vacuity assertions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All 178 bodies and every existing safety/fixed-point assertion remain covered with real pandoc.\n- [ ] Runtime evidence under the exact -n 3 --dist worksteal command shows one computation per required body/pass, with no per-worker duplicate cache fill.\n- [ ] No single test approaches the 300s hang guard under a contended macOS run.\n- [ ] Production renderer behavior and corpus thresholds are unchanged.\n- [ ] Coordinate with ashy-waterlog-hamadryas and dimmed-supersweet-xenarthra; neither previously approved removing corpus coverage.","id":"20cb-cbae-e9df-45e3","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["ci","performance","tests","jira","wiki"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Wiki corpus cost cache is duplicated by every xdist worker"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786598888076438001,"uuid":"bc7a87c4-127b-4df9-a24b-1caa23ea72a1"}